 "footnotes": [
  {
   "id": "c-eq-11-6-cited",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The book cites Eq. (11.6) here, and twice more for the ground state and excited state contributions worked out below. The equation meant each time is Eq. (9.65), the general solution for a coherent field."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-coherence",
   "kind": "correction",
   "html": "The overlap of the two components is $\\langle i\\kalphacoh|-i\\kalphacoh\\rangle = e^{-2|\\kalphacoh|^2}$, so the classical coherence $|\\langle\\hat{a}\\rangle|$ is at most of order $|\\kalphacoh|e^{-2|\\kalphacoh|^2}$; the book's $e^{-|\\kalphacoh|^2}$ lacks the factor 2 in the exponent. Either way it is exponentially small."
  },
  {
   "id": "c-fig-9-3",
   "kind": "correction",
   "figure": "sim-collapse-revival",
   "html": "The book's figure labels the revival $\\ktaurevival = \\kalphacoh/\\kg$. Eq. (9.71) gives $\\ktaurevival \\sim 2\\pi|\\kalphacoh|/\\kg$, which for $\\kalphacoh = 4$ is about $25/\\kg$."
  }
 ],
